{"id":27026,"path":"/vocabulary/a1/daily-routines-a1-english-vocabulary/","parentId":26178,"order":50,"section":"vocabulary","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Daily routines  – A1 English Vocabulary","seo":{"title":"Daily routines – A1 English Vocabulary - Test-English","description":"Learn basic English vocabulary about daily routines with our A1 lesson. It includes pictures, examples, exercises and games.","image":"/media/uploads/A1-English-Vocabulary_Daily-routine.jpg"},"modified":"2023-10-13T08:31:58","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h2>Daily routines</h2> <p>In this elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">vocabulary</a> lesson about Daily Routines, you will learn verb phrases used to talk about everyday activities. Check the explanation and do the exercises.</p> <hr> <h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option for each gap.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"990\"></div>","<h2>Daily routines</h2> <h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option to complete these sentences. You can use each option ONLY ONCE.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"991\"></div>","<h2>Daily routines</h2> <h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the sentences with the words from the box. Use each word ONLY ONCE</h5> <p><span class=\"textBox\">brush my teeth – do my homework – finish work – get dressed – go home – go shopping – go to work – have lunch – start work – wake up</span><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"992\"></div> <p></p>","<h2>Daily routines</h2> <h3>Exercise 4</h3> <h5>Match the sentences/pictures with the terms.</h5> <p></p> <h6>Reload the page to play again. Here’s a link to our <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/es/832340604/daily-routines-a1-vocabulary-flash-cards/?i=4i1uip&amp;x=1jqt\">Quizlet study set</a> about Daily Routines.</h6>"],"explanation":"<h2>Daily routines</h2> <p>In this A1 Elementary <a href=\"/vocabulary\">Vocabulary</a> Lesson about Daily Routines, you will learn verb phrases used to talk about everyday activities. Look at these pictures about everyday activities and read the text about a person’s daily routine.<br> <br> <img src=\"/media/uploads/Daily-routines_A1-vocabulary.png\" alt=\"Visual guide to daily routines vocabulary for A1 English learners.\" width=\"500\" height=\"1032\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-27092\" loading=\"lazy\"><br> </p> <div class=\"textBox\"> <p>Every day, I <span class=\"numPink\">1</span> <strong>wake up</strong> early in the morning. Then, I <span class=\"numPink\">2</span> <strong>get up</strong> and go to the bathroom to <span class=\"numPink\">3</span> <strong>brush my teeth</strong>. After that, I <span class=\"numPink\">4</span> <strong>have breakfast</strong> in the kitchen. I usually have some coffee and toast <strong>for</strong> breakfast. Next, I <span class=\"numPink\">5</span> <strong>have a shower</strong> and <span class=\"numPink\">6</span> <strong>get dressed</strong> for work.</p> <p>I usually <span class=\"numPink\">7</span> <strong>go to work</strong> by bus, but sometimes I walk. I <span class=\"numPink\">8</span> <strong>start work</strong> at 8 am At work, I <span class=\"numPink\">9</span> <strong>check my emails</strong> and do my tasks. At around 1 pm, I <span class=\"numPink\">10</span> <strong>have lunch</strong>, sometimes at work or at a nearby place.</p> <p>I <span class=\"numPink\">11</span> <strong>finish work</strong> at 5 pm, and after work, I <span class=\"numPink\">12</span> <strong>go home</strong>. In the evening, I <span class=\"numPink\">13</span> <strong>do homework</strong>,<span class=\"numPink\">14</span> <strong>go for a run</strong>, or <span class=\"numPink\">15</span> <strong>go to the gym</strong>. Sometimes, I <span class=\"numPink\">16</span> <strong>go shopping</strong> to buy things I need. Later, I <span class=\"numPink\">17</span> <strong>cook dinner</strong>. I always <span class=\"numPink\">18</span> <strong>have dinner</strong> with my family. Finally, I <span class=\"numPink\">19</span> <strong>watch TV</strong>, and when I’m tired, I <span class=\"numPink\">20</span> <strong>go to bed</strong>.</p> </div> <h3>Listen &amp; Practice: Vocabulary with Pronunciation</h3> <p>Here’s a video to help you review the vocabulary from this lesson and improve your pronunciation.</p> <div class=\"video-container\"> <div class=\"embed-container\"><div data-youtube=\"DnyOsjn7Ejk\"></div></div> </div> <div class=\"separator-dots\"><span>Flashcards</span></div> <p>After completing the exercises in this lesson on Daily Routines, you can use the unit’s <a href=\"https://quizlet.com/832340604\">Vocabulary Flashcards</a> to revise and help you memorize the terms.</p>","quizzes":[{"id":990,"questions":[{"id":8439,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>After I _____, I get dressed, and I go to work.</div>","choices":[{"id":14834,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> have breakfast</span>"},{"id":14835,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> have a shower</span>"},{"id":14836,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> finish work</span>"},{"id":14837,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> go shopping</span>"}]},{"id":8440,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ in the evening if there is a good series or film on.</div>","choices":[{"id":14838,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> watch TV</span>"},{"id":14839,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> eat breakfast</span>"},{"id":14840,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> start work</span>"},{"id":14841,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> sleep</span>"}]},{"id":8441,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>After I _____, I catch the bus home.</div>","choices":[{"id":14842,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> get up</span>"},{"id":14843,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> wake up</span>"},{"id":14844,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> start work</span>"},{"id":14845,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> finish work</span>"}]},{"id":8442,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I sometimes _____ in the park with my dog.</div>","choices":[{"id":14846,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> get up</span>"},{"id":14847,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> go shopping</span>"},{"id":14848,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> go running</span>"},{"id":14849,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> go to bed</span>"}]},{"id":8443,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I usually _____ at the kitchen table with my wife.</div>","choices":[{"id":14850,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> wake up</span>"},{"id":14851,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> have a shower</span>"},{"id":14852,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> have dinner</span>"},{"id":14853,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> brush my teeth</span>"}]},{"id":8444,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ at the desk in my bedroom after school.</div>","choices":[{"id":14854,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> get up</span>"},{"id":14855,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> do my homework</span>"},{"id":14856,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> finish work</span>"},{"id":14857,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> go shopping</span>"}]},{"id":8445,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I sometimes _____ at a café on my way to work.</div>","choices":[{"id":14858,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> get up</span>"},{"id":14859,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> have a shower</span>"},{"id":14860,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> have breakfast</span>"},{"id":14861,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> go running</span>"}]},{"id":8446,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>As soon as I _____, I get out of bed.</div>","choices":[{"id":14862,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> wake up</span>"},{"id":14863,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> have a shower</span>"},{"id":14864,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> have dinner</span>"},{"id":14865,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> brush my teeth</span>"}]},{"id":8447,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>After I have a shower, I _____ in my bedroom.</div>","choices":[{"id":14866,"letter":"A.","html":"<span> finish work</span>"},{"id":14867,"letter":"B.","html":"<span> go to the gym</span>"},{"id":14868,"letter":"C.","html":"<span> get dressed</span>"},{"id":14869,"letter":"D.","html":"<span> go shopping</span>"}]},{"id":8448,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I usually _____ by car, but sometimes I catch the bus.